WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.470
Are you all right, Nagomu-san?

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.870
You seem like you're having a tough time.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.870
I'm fine.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.080
I'm tired because my nose is 
still stuffed up. That's all.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.460
Mistress!

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:28.950
This is bad.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.760
It's up over 39 degrees.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.010
For real?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.070
Is your fever from exhaustion?

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.060
You should go see a doctor later.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.600
Yesterday...

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.180
You played games on your phone after your 
bath without drying your hair first, right?

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.310
Shh! Shh!

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.020
Go right now!

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:55.910
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.240
<b>Is It Good</b>

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.410
So, that idiot went and came back already?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.810
He was told it's just a cold, so I have 
him resting up on the second floor.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.410
Should I go call him down?

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.250
Huh? Call him?

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.460
Even in his state, he's worried about the shop.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.710
Really.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:44.380
Oh, wow! Without that giant lump in here, 
it's so much easier to move around!

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:48.270
I think that side of the master is quite cute.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.690
Masa-san...

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.900
<i>Dang it. He didn't have 
to say that so loud.</i>

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.820
<i>Today we had three orders 
for delivery, right?</i>

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:07.150
<i>Oh, that's right. I'm sure Kafuuen 
placed an order for twenty shitamoe.</i>

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.480
<i>I was supposed to take them over there.</i>

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:16.090
<i>Shitamoe, huh? Now I think about it, he also...</i>

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.610
Nagomu.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:20.590
Nagomu!

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.230
Hey! Hey, I said!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.430
<b>Modern Literature</b>

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.930
What's this?

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.250
Were you nodding off? Did you
 get tired of waiting?

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.030
Huh? Yeah.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:37.520
Hey, Nagomu. Can I stop 
by your place again today?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:44.270
Sorry I kept you waiting. The talk 
lasted longer than I thought it would.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.530
Talk? You mean about your career plans?

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.480
Senpai, you already decided to continue 
your education at Gokouzan, didn't you?

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.910
Yeah, that's right, but...

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.550
That's why you want to come to my place, huh?

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:58.050
Huh?

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:02.690
You said that when you have things to think
 about, you want to eat our sweets, right?

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:03.800
You remember that?

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.060
More than having things to think about, 
it's more of a personal superstition.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:14.810
I've probably already found my answer, 
but I need one more little push.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.360
The fact that our sweets 
provide that push is weird.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.150
Don't say that. A normal person would 
feel honored by something like that.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.640
You've got them right now, right? Shitamoe.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.920
I wanna eat one of those.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:33.040
Ryokushou's have matcha-flavored an, 
smooth an, and white an in three layers,

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.330
so when you eat it, three kinds of sweetness 
lightly bloom inside your mouth!

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.240
It's like when the snow melts.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.530
When I first ate one, I was truly moved.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:47.720
When you say things like that, it makes the 
artisans grateful to have been a part of it.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.970
Besides, eating those is how I met you, Nagomu.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.660
Oh, please!

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:57.630
Our sweets happened to be used in 
your etiquette class. That's all.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.120
It was just a coincidence.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.250
Idiot.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:04.310
That's what they call fate.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:12.040
Nagomu-san, I'll leave something 
for you to drink right here.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:17.750
<i>This is the first time I've been 
to the second floor of the shop.</i>

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:22.310
<i>I was worried about how he might be doing, 
so I asked the mistress to let me do this,</i>

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.760
Me! I'll take it to him!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.060
<i>but I wonder if I was too pushy about it.</i>

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.510
<i>I guess I'll redo his towel for him.</i>

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.770
<i>It's still warm.</i>

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:40.770
<i>If he opened his eyes right now...</i>

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.400
Mitsuru-chan, you stayed by my side?

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:45.820
Thank you.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.150
<i>Thank you... Thank you...</i>

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.640
<i>I can't handle it!</i>

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.910
<i>If he said that to me, 
I wouldn't be able to handle it!</i>

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.540
<i>But I want him to say it.</i>

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.560
<i>I-I don't think he hates me,</i>

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.520
<i>so making an appeal with kindness 
here would be okay, wouldn't it?</i>

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.700
<i>It would, right?</i>

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.060
<i>It would!</i>

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:04.510
<i>Then maybe, little by little, 
Nagomu-san's feelings would turn towards me.</i>

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.670
<i>And then...</i>

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.960
<i>We'd go shopping together...</i>

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.300
<i>He'd wait for me outside the school gates...</i>

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.320
<i>And when there were events, 
we'd spend the day together... Maybe?</i>

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:16.310
<i>No way! I'd be too happy! 
It would be terrible!</i>

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:21.690
<i>And then, one day, we'd spend all 
night in a guitar jam session...</i>

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:26.440
<i>No! Fantasizing any further would be too much!</i>

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.950
<i>Oh no! The voice of my heart 
escaped into the outside world!</i>

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.250
<i>And it was super loud!</i>

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.240
Nagomu-san, please get better soon.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.340
<b>Calligraphy Club</b>

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.340
<b>Japanese Archery</b>

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.340
<b>Congratulations on Your Admission
Come Play Hanafuda</b>

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:00.710
The way things are, it might be better 
to have Nagomu go do something else.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:06.250
<i>Must be nice, letting your 
sound ring out like that...</i>

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.320
You're the son of the couple that 
runs that wagashi shop, right?

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:13.160
The wagashi in today's etiquette class... 
They were from your place, right?

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.580
Where's your shop?

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.600
<i>He was the one playing guitar...</i>

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:21.580
In exchange for telling you where the 
shop is, please teach me to play guitar.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.100
You say some interesting things.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:32.720
<i>He said that, and then Senpai 
took me up on my deal.</i>

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:37.850
<b>Fuku Fuku Café</b>

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.710
<i>Talking with Senpai was so much fun.</i>

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:39.060
<i>Before I knew it, we were hanging 
out together all the time.</i>

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.340
<i>To me, Senpai became like family.</i>

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.780
Oh! You're here, huh?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:47.360
<b>Fuku Fuku</b>

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.360
Master! This guy is Nagomu.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.870
He's the son of the Ryokushou family.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:54.220
So, Master, you were my dad's classmate?

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.370
That's right. In high school.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.790
When did Senpai start working here?

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.620
It was right after Tomoe 
got into high school.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.580
And getting to the point where 
I could live on my own since then

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.000
is all thanks to the master here.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.520
<i>Senpai's parents had divorced early on,</i>

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.240
<i>and Senpai had gone with his mother, but...</i>

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.510
She got remarried, and I just couldn't 
get used to the new family.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.540
That was at the beginning of spring.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.640
You went by Ryokushou for 
the first time in a while.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.520
And on your way home, they made
 you take some sweets.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.760
What is this? It's yummy!

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.510
It's called "Shitamoe."

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:30.280
"Shitamoe"? What's it mean?

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:35.410
It's supposed to express sprouts breaking 
through the snow after a cold winter.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:40.870
Really? Then it's also an 
expression of hopefulness, right?

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.320
This guy had been agonizing over

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:47.690
whether he should move out 
when he became a second-year.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.590
After that, I left home almost immediately.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.470
You never know what'll serve 
as impetus for a change, right?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.300
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.970
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.210
I'm sorry, Kanoko-chan,

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:02.390
asking you to come pick up your order 
because we couldn't deliver it.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.890
What? Visit him?

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.900
That would be fine, but he might be asleep.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:13.240
You almost never catch a cold. What are 
you thinking, letting your guard down?

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:18.240
When we lived together, 
you did run a fever just once.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.640
Back then, you cried out in your sleep,

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:24.550
calling the name of the 
senpai you were looking for.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.520
Since the name was unisex, I was
 certain it was a woman's name,

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.090
and I hit you on the head 
really hard, didn't I?

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:37.590
You said, "If I keep playing 
guitar, I know I'll see him."

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.220
But compared to someone you couldn't
 find after ten years of searching,

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.350
don't you prefer me, who you found in three
 months without any searching at all?

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.250
Though just saying it is probably futile.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.800
Kanoko-chan! We have twenty 
shitamoe ready for you.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.960
Oh! Thank you!

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:57.920
I knew it. When I eat the old guy's wagashi,

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.910
it makes me feel like I've 
got my emotions sorted out.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:03.800
I look at it and ponder... 
Eat it and ponder...

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:05.660
Enjoy the afterglow and ponder...

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.170
And by the time I think, 
"Ah, that was delicious,"

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.830
all my unsettled feelings 
have been tidied up.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:18.380
So, you're not planning on ever coming back?

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.760
I don't know...

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:25.720
But if I ever need to make 
up my mind about something,

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.460
I'll come back to eat some sweets.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.270
Nagomu, thanks for everything up to now.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:33.400
I'll be leaving Kyoto ahead of you.

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:37.270
You should hurry up and 
decide on your future, too.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.330
Even if you say that to me...

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:48.000
<b>Kyoto Gokouzan University</b>

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:46.910
<i>In the end, I chose to go to university 
without thinking much of it.</i>

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:49.770
<i>And without thinking much of it,
 I continued playing guitar.</i>

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:51.980
<i>And I still had fun doing it. But...</i>

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:55.450
<i>I couldn't fill the sense of emptiness 
that smoldered in my heart.</i>

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:01.150
<i>"I know! Maybe Senpai will 
be able to fill this hole."</i>

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:04.950
<i>"If I follow the path Senpai 
was aiming for, then..."</i>

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.850
<i>"Somewhere under this sky..."</i>

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:11.860
<i>"I wonder... Is Senpai 
still playing his music?"</i>

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.120
Cold!

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:15.860
Huh?

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.710
Itsuka?

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:21.200
Obachan asked me to come change your towel.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.750
Huh? Is this one you just wrung out?

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.330
It's super cold.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.360
She told me to use the ones she'd 
chilled ice cold in the freezer.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:28.620
That's bad for my heart!

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:33.250
Now I'm exhausted. I was dreaming,
 and now I'm tired.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:37.660
What kind of dream was it? Sorting azuki 
beans for all eternity or something?

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.240
That would be a nightmare.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:43.160
I had a senpai who loved our sweets.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.570
I asked that senpai to teach me guitar.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:50.780
I was having a dream about 
when we said farewell.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:55.640
I searched while I was in 
Tokyo, but no luck there.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:01.160
But, well, I guess my 
timing might've been off.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:09.120
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:09.120
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.600
After seeing it in my dream, I remembered...

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:10.760
Senpai said, "If I ever need to make up 
my mind about something, I'll come back."

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:17.250
Maybe when that happens, Senpai 
will eat a sweet I made.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:21.390
That would be a great way to reunite, right?

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:22.490
I'm so happy for you.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:22.970
Huh?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.660
To be so optimistic in the face of 
such indefinite variables...

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:26.920
Those eyes...

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.720
They're colder than the towel was!

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.580
Oh! It's snowing.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.440
<i>Today is February 13th.</i>

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:44.280
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:44.280
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:43.610
<i>The weather in the southern part of 
Kyoto is cloudy with occasional snow.</i>

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.280
<i>Due to the winter pressure patterns, 
a cold wave is coming...</i>

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.430
<i>and the whole country is likely 
to experience deepening cold.</i>

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.540
Snow, huh?

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.500
<i>The snowfall that begins this afternoon 
will continue into early morning...</i>

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.950
They said it'd be about 
the same as two years ago.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.870
Is your cold better now?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.510
I'm fine. Don't worry. 
I've got energy to spare.

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.590
The snow has been falling 
lightly up until now, but...

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:04.220
I wish I could've seen all 
the snow two years ago.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.010
If only I'd been here.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.050
"What ifs" are unproductive.

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:10.810
It's already passed, after all.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.400
Well, that's true, but...

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:15.310
Huh? Did you add mochi to this sumashi soup?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:18.280
I had some frozen ones 
left over from Shogatsu.

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.060
I have to use them up somehow.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.550
Then, how about on our break, 
we use some to make zenzai soup?

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:24.480
It'll warm us up, too.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:25.650
What a good idea.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:28.990
And we still have shio kombu that 
we got as a year-end gift, right?

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.760
Let's do that.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.300
Would you all like to eat some, too?

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.580
We'll have some, thank you.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.760
What about you, Itsuka?

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:38.030
Should I set some aside to warm up for 
you after you get back from school?

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:39.840
I won't have any, thank you.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.900
Then you should make it, Nagomu.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:42.330
Huh?

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.410
You should be able to make 
something like that for everyone.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:45.510
And you suggested it, right?

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.050
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:49.070
You're already apologizing?

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:50.600
How gallant of you.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.600
<b>Furled
Crimson</b>

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.600
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.920
One Hearts Entwined set, please.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:56.100
<b>Hearts Entwined Set
 • Chocolate yokan
 • Matcha manju
 • Jouyo manju
 • Wasanbon sugar</b>

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.100
Thank you.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.400
Hello.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.610
Oh, Kanoko-chan. Welcome.

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:05.040
We got our spring fliers, so I was 
asked to bring some to leave here.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.680
Thank you for your hard work. I'll take them.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.450
Oh, dear! Your hands look so cold!

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:15.450
It's especially cold today. 
I should have worn gloves.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:19.160
I'll bring you some warm 
zenzai soup. Rest a little.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:22.880
No, I couldn't! I still have to go 
to a few more places after this!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.680
Well, then, all the more so.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:28.140
The furthest table is open. 
Hurry up and go sit down.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.520
Th-Thank you.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.640
<i>Oh, that's so cute!</i>

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:37.350
<i>Right, tomorrow is Valentine's.</i>

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:41.600
<i>I wish I was delivering the 
flyers tomorrow instead.</i>

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:45.750
<i>That way, it would have been easier to 
give him something "since I was here."</i>

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.860
Hey. Thanks for your hard work.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.140
Nagomu!

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.120
One zenzai soup. Thanks for waiting.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.510
How's your cold? Are you feeling better?

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.780
Yeah. I'm all better.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.060
Come on. Eat up.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:00.620
Okay. Thank you for the treat!

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.560
Oh, it's delicious!

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.520
I was feeling chilled, 
and this warmed me right up.

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.550
I heard you have other 
places to go to after this?

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:12.220
That's right.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.910
If you get cold again, 
come back and have some more.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:17.360
We'll give you a decent batch next time.

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:17.970
What?

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:21.880
It's just... that's a batch 
I made for the staff.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:24.310
You mean you made this yourself?

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.920
Kanoko's here? I'll give her some!

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:28.010
Adding water, then anko, then water again...

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:28.950
Why did you make it in a stockpot?

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:30.300
I ended up with an insane amount, you see.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.490
I am technically a customer, you know.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:36.160
To make up for it, we won't charge you 
anything for it. Rest as long as you like.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:36.910
Later!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:37.950
Thank you!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:38.660
Sure.

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.100
<i>Homemade, huh?</i>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.300
<b>Easy Chocolate Chiffon Cake</b>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.300
<b>Easy</b>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.300
<b>Homemade Chocolate Chiffon Cake</b>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.300
<b>For Hand Piping
 Fondant Chocolate</b>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.300
<b>"When you want to give homemade chocolate."</b>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.300
<b>Melts in your mouth!
 Couverture Chocolate</b>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.300
<i>I'm just challenging myself. 
Just challenging myself...</i>

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:55.760
<i>That's right. I just wanted to give it a 
try as a sort of thank you. That's all.</i>

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.010
Itsuka-chan!

00:15:58.400 --> 00:15:59.820
Kanoko-san!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:01.980
Are you playing hooky from work?

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:02.990
You're so mean.

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:05.270
I-I'm working just like I should be!

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.280
Would that be chocolate?

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:09.390
Huh? Yes. Well, you know...

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:13.360
Some for people who look out for me, 
some for friends, some for me...

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.530
It was fun looking for all the things, so...

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.890
They have wagashi for 
Valentine's Day, too, don't they?

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:21.540
The ones at Ryokushou made me think, 
"Oh, how cute," when I saw them.

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:26.040
But wagashi feel more like special event 
things than fun event things, don't you think?

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:29.500
Itsuka-chan, did you buy chocolate? 
For a guy you like or something?

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.160
Huh? I don't have anyone.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.920
What? You don't have anyone like that?

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:33.930
What about for Nagomu?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.050
Huh? Hold off with that face.

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:39.640
I did buy some for the 
people I want to thank.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.680
I see.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:42.850
Oh...

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:45.820
Snow.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.920
It's finally started falling.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:54.440
Itsuka-chan?

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:55.150
Huh?

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:58.530
Is something wrong? You seemed 
to space out a little.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.350
No, I'm fine.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.540
Oh, okay.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.620
It just keeps piling up.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.500
Hey.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:26.810
The day Itsuka came, it was 
snowing like this, right?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.310
That's right.

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:31.050
The sight of the two of 
them standing there...

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:34.060
I can still see it as though 
it happened just yesterday.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.560
Why the sudden interest in that?

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.480
Just... Today, when Itsuka 
came home through the snow,

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:41.870
something about her expression bothered me.

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:51.400
<i>It's still snowing.</i>

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.670
<i>Just like that day...</i>

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:01.530
I'm home, Papa!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.560
Welcome back, Itsuka.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:19.600
Papa, when it piles up some more, 
I want to make one this big!

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.100
What?

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.570
A snowman!

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:25.690
We made one before when we 
went to the ski place, right?

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.400
You're right...

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:32.460
That was so much fun, right, Papa?

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.020
Yeah, it was.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:38.990
Hey, Itsuka.

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:43.530
The zenzai soup we had that 
time was good, wasn't it?

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:44.390
Huh?

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.730
Should we go have some? I know 
a place where it's delicious.

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:51.720
<i>If, back then...</i>

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:54.980
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:54.980
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.070
<i>I hadn't said, "Okay"...</i>

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:04.600
<i>If, back then...</i>

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.700
<b>To the nice man and lady from Ryokushou,</b>

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.700
<b>Please take care of this girl.</b>

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.700
<b>Sorry, Itsuka</b>

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.910
<i>Papa hadn't left me...</i>

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:11.790
I told you.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.850
Kids only get in the way.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.790
They're a handful...

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:17.270
and they're no help with anything.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.550
<i>Papa?</i>

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:28.220
How long are you gonna 
stay like that, Itsuka?

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.840
It's super amazing outside!

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:33.980
Come on out!

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.730
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.730
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:48.620
I haven't seen this much snow 
on the ground since I was a kid!

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.000
It was piled up like this 
two years ago, though.

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:53.230
Gloves. Here.

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:54.710
What should we make? What should we make?

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.190
Is there a reason I have to do this?

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.970
You could just do it on 
your own, couldn't you?

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.990
Snow is cold, and it's freezing out here.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:06.700
<i>And I feel lonely...</i>

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:10.110
Itsuka, when you first came here, 
it was a snowy day like today, right?

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:10.730
Huh?

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:15.480
If I'd been here, what would we have 
played together? I couldn't help wondering.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.350
What?

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:20.730
Really, when I heard about it, 
I thought about what a shame it was.

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:24.950
I definitely would have said, "Itsuka, 
let's go play!" and taken you outside.

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:28.860
Why are you assuming that I'd go play?

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:31.510
It's my imagination. What's the harm?

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:35.020
"What ifs" might be unproductive,

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:37.900
but if you get a chance to do it over,

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.240
then you should, right?

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.350
Say, Itsuka...

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:44.710
Want to play?

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:51.980
I don't know if the me from 
two years ago would say yes.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.680
Well, yeah, that's true, but...

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:56.730
Huh?

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:01.990
I suppose I wouldn't mind making a snowman.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:03.740
Great!

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.010
Then, I'll make your face, Itsuka!

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:09.560
If you make it ugly, I'm going to be angry!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.000
What are you two doing?!

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.120
Honestly, you've both gotten so cold!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.000
And, Nagomu, you have prep work to do!

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:21.260
And I don't have time to heat 
the bath at this time of day!

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:22.810
Oh! Let's grill up some mochi.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:23.950
Mochi?!

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:26.010
There's some zenzai soup 
left over from yesterday.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.760
I'll warm it up and eat it.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.140
Itsuka, you should have some, too.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:32.230
You're having something 
like that before breakfast?

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:33.770
Well...

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.030
Just a little.

00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:14.490
It's only snowing a little now.

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.680
Yes, but it really snowed a lot, didn't it?

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:19.500
And we're already halfway through February.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:20.570
Halfway?

00:23:20.570 --> 00:23:22.640
Huh? What's the date today, again?

00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:23.500
Huh?

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:25.740
I have this sweet sort of image in my head...

00:23:25.740 --> 00:23:28.700
Like a trick-or-treat sort of thing...

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:30.640
At the very least,

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:34.010
I don't think it's a day where adults 
should be sponging off of children.

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:38.520
You're the one who demanded it. 
Why are you making that face?

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:41.190
Well, if I don't leave soon, I'll be late.

00:23:44.870 --> 00:23:46.090
I'm going now.

00:23:47.270 --> 00:23:48.570
Come back safe!

00:23:49.940 --> 00:24:09.960
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:49.940 --> 00:24:09.960
<b>"Red Sea Bream for a Spring Dawn"</b>

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.830
What are you doing?

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:58.830
It's almost here.

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:58.830
<b>Exclusively for Nagomu-san
3/26
Going Somewhere Together
 Ticket</b>

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:08.940
If the father could move a 
little more toward the center...

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:09.960
The father?!
